    "long_instructions": "<div style=\"background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;\">\r\n<p>📖 <b>A Computer System</b> is a set of parts that work together to process information and complete tasks. It includes:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0;\">• <b>Hardware:</b> the physical parts</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0;\">• <b>Software:</b> the programs that run on it</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0;\">• <b>Operating System:</b> manages the hardware and software</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p>Computer systems are everywhere in daily life, from smartphones and gaming consoles to self-checkout kiosks, smart home devices, and even AI-powered cars.</p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #D5EFFF; color: #06338D; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;\">\r\n<p>🔎 <b>Think About:</b> as you watch, listen for how the different parts of a computer system, hardware, software, and the operating system, work together.</p>\r\n</div>"
  },
